WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.621 --> 00:00:05.364
DeskPack for Adobe Photoshop

00:00:05.526 --> 00:00:08.361
brings flexo expertise
right to your desktop,

00:00:08.774 --> 00:00:10.681
in your favorite
retouching application.

00:00:11.491 --> 00:00:14.953
With Viewer, you get a color-accurate
preview of your image,

00:00:15.461 --> 00:00:17.229
whether printed
in process inks,

00:00:17.413 --> 00:00:19.521
spot inks
or a combination.

00:00:20.081 --> 00:00:22.429
You see your image
exactly as it will print,

00:00:22.846 --> 00:00:25.241
reducing the need
for intermediate proofs.

00:00:26.003 --> 00:00:27.863
With the multichannel densitometer,

00:00:27.976 --> 00:00:30.008
you can place
multiple measuring points

00:00:30.171 --> 00:00:32.361
on the critical areas
in your image.

00:00:32.898 --> 00:00:35.013
This gives you
live numeric feedback,

00:00:35.173 --> 00:00:36.721
while you’re editing the image.

00:00:37.590 --> 00:00:41.241
Minimum dots and highlight breaks
require special attention.

00:00:41.884 --> 00:00:46.561
Viewer simulates this behavior on plate
and on press to catch errors early.

00:00:47.201 --> 00:00:49.441
You can see where
gradations break off

00:00:49.803 --> 00:00:53.801
and check whether your images have been
properly adapted to your flexo press.

00:00:54.351 --> 00:00:57.883
Viewer also highlights
Total Area Coverage or TAC

00:00:58.184 --> 00:01:02.481
to see areas where the ink coverage
of your image exceeds a given limit.

00:01:03.199 --> 00:01:05.481
This reduces problems
with ink trapping,

00:01:05.776 --> 00:01:09.041
giving you cleaner images
and fewer problems on press.

00:01:09.841 --> 00:01:13.881
Many of your images may be separated
and retouched for offset printing.

00:01:14.413 --> 00:01:17.841
But what if the same images
now need to be printed in flexo?

00:01:18.453 --> 00:01:21.961
FlexoFix helps you convert
your images for flexo printing.

00:01:22.653 --> 00:01:25.488
Unlike other curve or
color management approaches,

00:01:25.928 --> 00:01:28.113
FlexoFix analyzes your images

00:01:28.343 --> 00:01:30.948
and then applies
context-sensitive changes.

00:01:31.453 --> 00:01:33.681
This helps to eliminate
the most common issues

00:01:33.844 --> 00:01:37.681
while still preserving the fidelity
and saturation of the image.

00:01:38.281 --> 00:01:42.321
The FlexoClean filter works just
like any other filter in Photoshop.

00:01:42.829 --> 00:01:44.961
You can automatically
remove scum dots

00:01:45.124 --> 00:01:47.761
and fill in small holes
with minimum dots.

00:01:48.333 --> 00:01:50.923
With FlexoClean,
you get cleaner printing plates

00:01:51.086 --> 00:01:53.201
and excellent on-press quality.

00:01:53.881 --> 00:01:56.161
Your images are setup
for process printing

00:01:56.324 --> 00:01:59.721
but your packaging also
uses spot or brand colors.

00:02:00.359 --> 00:02:03.959
What if you could replace some
of the process inks with your spot inks,

00:02:04.121 --> 00:02:06.401
without changing the way
the image looks?

00:02:06.791 --> 00:02:08.841
That’s what InkSwitch
has to offer.

00:02:09.459 --> 00:02:11.576
Based on Esko
color management,

00:02:11.666 --> 00:02:14.763
InkSwitch analyzes
the full gamut of your image

00:02:14.924 --> 00:02:17.881
and calculates a new set
of spot color separations

00:02:18.044 --> 00:02:19.881
that match
the original image.

00:02:20.513 --> 00:02:23.681
InkSwitch is the spot color
tool for Photoshop.

00:02:24.273 --> 00:02:26.993
InkSwitch helps you keep
the number of inks to a minimum,

00:02:27.431 --> 00:02:28.896
reducing your ink usage

00:02:29.056 --> 00:02:31.081
and saving you
both time and money.

00:02:31.726 --> 00:02:34.515
You get better quality
from your spot color images:

00:02:34.861 --> 00:02:36.163
better color balance,

00:02:36.276 --> 00:02:39.600
better solid ink densities
and better dot gain control.

00:02:40.243 --> 00:02:41.828
With DeskPack for Photoshop,

00:02:41.988 --> 00:02:43.640
you can detect
problems earlier,

00:02:43.799 --> 00:02:46.601
reducing your costs and
saving you valuable time.

00:02:47.305 --> 00:02:49.794
Your learning curve is short
and training costs are low

00:02:49.958 --> 00:02:54.361
because the plug-ins have the same look
and feel as the rest of Adobe Photoshop.

00:02:55.176 --> 00:02:58.081
You can prepare your images
for flexo printing faster,

00:02:58.244 --> 00:03:00.620
with better quality
and fewer errors.

00:03:01.261 --> 00:03:04.061
DeskPack for Photoshop
makes you the expert.

